<article class="env-lemma" id="0B05">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0B05">Lemma <span data-tag="0B05">43.16.4</span>.</a> In Lemma <a href="/tag/0B04" data-tag="0B04">43.16.3</a> assume that $c = 1$, i.e., $V$ is an effective Cartier divisor. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  e(X, V \cdot W, Z) = \text{length}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }} (\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi }/f_1\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi }).  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      In this case the image of $f_1$ in $\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi }$ is nonzero by properness of intersection, hence a nonzerodivisor divisor. Moreover, $\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi }$ is a Noetherian local domain of dimension $1$. Thus 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \text{length}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }} (\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi }/f_1^ t\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi }) = t \text{length}_{\mathcal{O}_{X, \xi }} (\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi }/f_1\mathcal{O}_{W, \xi })  \]
</div>
    <p>
       for all $t \geq 1$, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/02MC" data-tag="02MC">10.121.1</a>. This proves the lemma. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>